  "what_this_still_cannot_settle": [
    "Career stage, and not for want of controls: within a player, calendar year and career year are collinear by construction, so their linear effects are not separately identifiable. The year coefficient is a compound of scale drift and mean career trajectory. This is the age-period-cohort problem and it is structural, not a sample-size issue.",
    "Selection into TWIC. Appearing in tournament reports at all is not random, and a player's TWIC games are not their full year.",
    "Engine drift is not at issue (one fixed Stockfish build, fixed nodes), but the anchor is still ACPL, which measures one aspect of play quality rather than skill in general."
  ]
}